  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Nature&#x2019;s Principles customer acquisition tests</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Nature&apos;s Principles developed technology for the sustainable production of lactic acid through an innovative fermentation processes using waste streams for any sugar and ethanol production processes.
They are not yet in the commercial phase. Customers want to see proof that this innovative solution works. TA subsidy to support the needed activities. 
Sugar/ethanol producers are often very big industry parties who have many sugar waste streams. Nature&#x2019;s Principles has technology to use this &#x2018;waste&#x2019; and get (highly valuable) lactic acid out of it. 
Lactic acid has applications for food (as preservative, it suppress bacteria), pharma (used in drugs), agri-chemicals (enhances soil fertility and nutrient uptake), and production of Bioplastics. 
Lactic acid (melkzuur) can be produced fermentation of carbohydrates (carbs; koolhydraten) a.k.a. sugar (glucose). Nature&#x2019;s Principles has created technology to produce lactic acid from &#x201c;complex&#x201d; feedstock/carbohydrates, basically a mix of all kinds of waste, in stead of a &#x2018;homogeneous&#x2019; waste &#x2013; which is hard to find in reality). The &#x2018;complex carbohydrates&#x2019; is currently just &#x2018;normal waste&#x2019; for big industrial parties. 
Currently lactic acid is now produced only from simple sugar crops like sugarbeets. But for Nature&#x2019;s Principles it&#x2019;s possible to use much more, and more complex, sugar waste streams. And in a much more sustainable (chemicals; energy use) way.</narrative>
  </description>
